Hannah (docs): Quick sync — found a support ticket where customers see a 429 after the SDK streamed a partial assistant chunk. Our docs say "trim and retry" but we should show a practical pattern that: 1) logs partial output, 2) avoids duplicate side-effects, 3) trims safely (no system drops), and 4) retries respecting Retry-After. Can we add a tiny example and a short migration note?

Ravi (sdk): I can add a compact snippet. Two quick decisions: message-level trimming only, and include a guard to persist the last-acknowledged assistant id so UI doesn't re-run side-effects for partial responses.

Kai (eng-runtime): Runtime now sets x-partial-ok=1 and includes x-partial-offset when streaming cut off. SDK exposes err.partialOffset and err.partialText. Recommend logging those and returning an explicit flag to the app so it can reconcile. Also, honor Retry-After >= 1s otherwise backoff.

Jules (devex): We'll need two tiny UX strings for the callout: 'Received partial replyreconciling...' and 'Retrying trimmed request...'. I can add locales after merge.

Ravi (sdk): Draft JS example (compact):

```js
// on partial/429: log partial, trim oldest non-system turns, retry
async function sendStreamSafe(client, convo){
  let seenId = convo.meta?.lastAckedId;
  for(let attempt=0; attempt<3; attempt++){
    try { return await client.generate({conversation:convo}); }
    catch(e){
      if(e.status!==429) throw e;
      if(e.partialText) console.info('partial:', e.partialText, 'offset', e.partialOffset);
      const ra=parseFloat(e.headers?.['retry-after']||'0');
      await sleep(ra>=1?ra*1000:Math.pow(2,attempt)*300 + Math.random()*80);
      while(convo.length && tokenCount(convo)>2500){ if(convo[0].role==='system') break; convo.shift(); }
      // preserve lastAckedId so UI can avoid duplicating side-effects
      convo.meta = {...convo.meta, lastAckedId: seenId};
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}
```

Ravi (sdk): I'll also add a Swift snippet in the SDK repo docs since mobile customers asked.

Kai (eng-runtime): Add bold callout: DO NOT DROP system/instruction messages. Also add an operator note: "x-partial-offset > 0 means some tokens were emitted; reconcile before replaying mutations."

Hannah (docs): Perfect. I'll keep the docs insertion tiny — a 3-line explanation + snippet + 1-line migration tip: "Switch ad-hoc retry code to sdk.retryUtils.trimAndRetry to get uniform behavior across languages."

